menuconfig MESHTASTIC_LED_STATUS
	bool "Board LED says whether the node is in use (bench diagnostic)"
	default n
	depends on GPIO
	depends on !MESHTASTIC_EXTNOTIFY
	help
	  Drives the board LED(s) directly, independent of the Meshtastic
	  app/config, to answer the bench's question at a glance: which of
	  these identical boards is in a test, which is free, and which one is
	  the node called rzr5. The host sets the mode from the bench's claims
	  (`meshtastic led mode ...`, tools/leds.sh); the node remembers it.

	    idle     slow blink (red on a XIAO)       -- free, available
	    in-use   solid green on a XIAO, off on a one-LED board
	    locate   fast blink (blue on a XIAO) for a while, then back
	    off      dark

	  A board with green and blue LEDs (led1/led2, the XIAO's RGB) uses the
	  colours; a board with one LED (the Heltecs' white led0) uses the
	  patterns alone.

	  Mutually exclusive with CONFIG_MESHTASTIC_EXTNOTIFY: both want sole
	  ownership of led0, and this module does not arbitrate with it.

if MESHTASTIC_LED_STATUS

config MESHTASTIC_LED_STATUS_LOCATE_SEC
	int "Default locate duration (s)"
	default 30
	range 1 600
	help
	  How long `meshtastic led locate` blinks when no duration is given.

endif # MESHTASTIC_LED_STATUS
